WEBVTT

00:05:57.604 --> 00:06:00.682
So the theory is that he's having
some immunological reaction

00:06:00.706 --> 00:06:03.121
to what's going on --
to the food, essentially.

00:06:03.145 --> 00:06:06.515
And that's a natural reaction,
which causes some programmed cell death,

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:08.809
but the gene that regulates
that down is broken.

00:06:08.833 --> 00:06:11.251
And so this informs,
among other things, of course,

00:06:11.275 --> 00:06:14.246
a treatment for bone marrow transplant,
which he undertakes.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.290
And after nine months
of grueling recovery,

00:06:16.314 --> 00:06:18.219
he's now eating steak with A1 sauce.

00:06:18.243 --> 00:06:19.340
(Laughter)

00:06:19.364 --> 00:06:23.463
The prospect of using the genome
as a universal diagnostic

00:06:23.487 --> 00:06:25.027
is upon us today.

00:06:26.202 --> 00:06:27.741
Today. It's here.

00:06:27.765 --> 00:06:29.257
And what it means for all of us

00:06:29.281 --> 00:06:32.568
is that everybody in this room
could live an extra 5, 10, 20 years,